From f5fb89cb5ea1f322a62d6c1a3e40d933cecdf5ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bugcheck <bugcheck@local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:29:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Trees: off the sidewalk walking lines, none inside buildings
 or on park paths

Yasin 7 Nov: many trees on pedestrian ways; some buildings have trees (and soil) in them.
Data change only (trees.json, no code, no cell package re-bake: trees are placed and drawn at runtime
from these rows; the cached placement furn_trees_place is keyed by the file's md5 and is rebuilt by
the furniture bake or at load). Offline scan (bugcheck1/tools/tree_scan.gd) of all 21274 trees:
- 376 inside a building: a LOD0 roof triangle (818 building chunks, 46994 roof tris) >= 2.2 m above
  the trunk base -> removed
- 109 on a park / footway path (terrain class 15) -> removed
- 1609 within 1.0 m of a crowd walk graph sidewalk line: 1524 moved ~1 m out of the walking space
  (same side first, never onto the road (+1.35 m), into a building or onto a path); 85 with no free
  spot beside them removed
Every removal is in trees.json 'removed' with its reason (20704 trees left). test_tree_col PASS.
---
 map_dc/coronado/furniture/data/trees.json | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

